Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:23:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ACCOUNTS-3: an account with a balance closes only at nil

Net worth counts open accounts only, while the budget counts them all, so
closing an account with money in it took the money off the statement and
left it in Ready to Assign. 50,000 in the bank and 20,000 owed on a card is
a net worth of 30,000; closing both made it 0, and Ready to Assign still
read 50,000. docs/accounts.md promised a warning; there was none. The
generic close also bypassed WEALTH-30's refusal on a family loan's own
tracking account.

closeAccount now refuses a budget, credit, plain tracking or family-loan
account whose ledger balance is not nil, naming the amount. The simulation
exercises close and reopen on an empty account instead of a funded one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
